--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Notifications/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app targets
list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,
shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real, compiled canonical
page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**` — where the sibling P7
notifications/AuditLog page (and ApiPlayground, DiskForecast, …) ship and which `Sources`
already lists as a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore
ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Notifications/**`, the faithful equivalent of the
prompt's `Features/Notifications`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the same
reconciliation the sibling notifications-AuditLog log recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/notifications/webhooks` is nested. A dedicated
`.notificationsWebhooks` AppRoute case is added (pathSegment `notifications/webhooks` →
`.path` `/notifications/webhooks` matching web exactly; Operations group alongside
`.notifications` + `.notificationsAudit`; icon `point.3.connected.trianglepath.dotted` —
the same SF Symbol WebhookGlyph.webhook the section header uses), `AppRouteParser` aliases
`/notifications/webhooks` → `.notificationsWebhooks` (required — the generic first-segment
fallback would otherwise resolve `.notifications`), and `WebhooksRouteRegistration` hosts the
page, chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift right after the notifications-AuditLog
registration. So the page is reachable via the Operations-group sidebar entry and any
`/notifications/webhooks` deep link. (Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

