DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI WebhooksPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable
WebhooksPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the two web i18n keys the page renders, the
copy-link share URL (web copyLink), and the embedded WebhookChannelsSectionModel built over an injectable
WebhookChannelsSource seam (production binds the shared KMP useWebhookChannels query through the seam). The
page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + copyLink) and hosts the already-shipped
WebhookChannelsSection feature view (its own P4 parity unit) — reused, not re-implemented (DRY) — so every web
data state (loading / empty / error / stale / offline / content), the add/edit form, the delete confirm, the
per-row test/toggle, and the HMAC signature preview render natively. A dedicated `.notificationsWebhooks` route
(pathSegment `notifications/webhooks`, Operations group) + parser alias + registration make it sidebar-reachable
and `/notifications/webhooks` deep-linkable, preserving every RouteTests invariant (verified by the route
harness). Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0/0 + iOS 0/0, incl.
previews) and the executed model + route harness (all assertions passed). The full xcodebuild scheme was NOT run
— it is gated on the out-of-scope, P1-owned KMP `Shared.xcframework` Gradle staging that OOM-kills this shared
host (per the sibling log), and triggering it would be irresponsible on a shared runner; deferred to its owner /
